=== QA FINDING F3 (minor, presenter-facing) — §D4's 'seven containers' ===
RUNBOOK.md:686-687 says: "Point at the running stack as proof of (1): docker compose -f
demo/docker-compose.yml ps — seven containers, none of them Maestro."

Typed exactly as written, that command prints SIX rows. kafka-init has run and exited, and
plain 'ps' lists only running containers; it takes 'ps -a' to see seven.
  docker compose -f demo/docker-compose.yml ps      -> 6 rows
  docker compose -f demo/docker-compose.yml ps -a   -> 7 rows
The compose file does define seven services (grafana jaeger kafka kafka-init postgres
prometheus valkey) so the number is not wrong — the command shown under it does not produce it.
A presenter says 'seven' while the room counts six on the projector.

